  "title": "Decrease Elements To Make Array Zigzag",
  "category": "dsa",
  "subcategory": "greedy",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Greedy"
  ],
  "statement": "Given an array `nums` of integers, a _move_ consists of choosing any element and **decreasing it by 1**.\n\nAn array `A` is a _zigzag array_ if either:\n\n*   Every even-indexed element is greater than adjacent elements, ie. `A[0] > A[1] < A[2] > A[3] < A[4] > ...`\n*   OR, every odd-indexed element is greater than adjacent elements, ie. `A[0] < A[1] > A[2] < A[3] > A[4] < ...`\n\nReturn the minimum number of moves to transform the given array `nums` into a zigzag array.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: We can decrease 2 to 0 or 3 to 1.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [9,6,1,6,2]\nOutput: 4\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= nums.length <= 1000",
    "1 <= nums[i] <= 1000"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "nums = [1,2,3]",
      "output": "2",
      "explanation": "We can decrease 2 to 0 or 3 to 1."
    },
    {
      "input": "nums = [9,6,1,6,2]",
      "output": "4",
      "explanation": null
    }
  ],
